{
  "slug": "statsclaw",
  "name": "Statsclaw",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "StatsClaw orchestrates 9 specialized AI agents (leader, planner, builder, tester, scriber, simulator, distiller, reviewer, shipper) through 13 workflows — from simple code changes to Monte Carlo simulation studies. Features include two-pipeline isolation for adversarial verification, automatic credential detection, shared knowledge brain system, and workspace-synced audit logs. Users just describe what they want in plain language; the leader agent handles the rest.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **15 skills** and **9 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (15): `attribution` (Commit authorship policy — no co-author trailers, user is sole author), `brain-sync` (Knowledge sharing lifecycle management), `contribute` (Session knowledge contribution to the shared brain), `credential-setup` (Automatic GitHub credential detection and verification), `handoff` (Artifact handoff protocol for two-pipeline architecture), `isolation` (Two-pipeline isolation protocol (worktree and information-level)), `issue-patrol` (Automated GitHub issue scanning, triage, and fix loop), `mailbox` (Inter-agent mailbox communication protocol), and 7 more\n- **Agents** (9): `builder` (Code Pipeline — implements source code from spec.md), `distiller` (Knowledge Extraction & Privacy Scrub — proposes brain contributions), `leader` (Team Leader — plans work, dispatches specialist teammates, manages state), `planner` (Requirements Analyst — produces spec.md, test-spec.md, and sim-spec.md), `reviewer` (Pipeline Convergence & Quality Gate — cross-compares all pipelines), `scriber` (Recording, Documentation & Architecture — sole owner of all docs), `shipper` (Git and GitHub Operations — commits, pushes, PRs, issue comments), `simulator` (Monte Carlo Simulation Pipeline — DGP design and execution), and 1 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install statsclaw@claude-community` from `statsclaw/statsclaw`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
